Python VS MEL
- no clear advantage to MEL.
- MEL was developed 20 years ago and not updated, only for Maya
- python is general purpose and continually developing
- python had robust libraries and countless 3rd party packages
- python is the standard VFX industry language (Houdini, Nuke, etc)
- Basic MEL understanding is still important as Maya UI is built with MEL
- Should know how to interpret MEL commands as actions are output as MEL

Python Versions and Maya
- python 3 is not backwards compatible with python 2

Scripting Environment
- quickest way to execute command is through the command line
- command line can be hidden, fix with (Window > UI Elements > Command Line)
- Type button (MEL, Python) toggles which language is being used
- Script Editor (Windows > General Editors > Script Editor), or UI Button bottom right
- Script Editor has two sections (output/history, and code)
- Add new MEL or Python tabs to code window
- Use keyboard enter to execute written code
- Maya for some reason deletes your code after executing, to avoid this highlight your code (Ctrl+A) then keyboard enter
- This odd behaviour makes using the script editor undesirable outside of testing tiny code snippets
- Results are only displayed when a single line of code is executed. To view results more reliably wrap them in a print()

