Maya Commands (Part 1)
- python wrapper for MEL
- commands can be parameterized, noted as 'Flags' which is what MEL calls them
- to see all parameters for a command in editor use the cmds.help("commandName")


Maya Commands (Part 2)
- edit and query flags are special, these indicate the 'mode' of the command
- if no mode is specified then the default mode is 'create'
- query will return the current value of a property
- edit will update the value of the property
- when an object is not specified in the command call, current selection will be used (if nothing selected then error)
- object name can be passed as first arg
- querying only allows one value to be queried at a time
- using commands on incorrect object types will raise errors (cmds.PolySphere() on a polyCube object)

Maya Commands (Part 3)
- the two most common commands are list (cmds.ls()) and select (cmds.select())

